+## v1.3.1 completion-scope guidance
+
+Use `completion_scope` only when needed to distinguish a task not directly attached to a mandatory requirement:
+
+- `REQUIRED`: a task whose incomplete status should block the scoped G5 result, including a supporting operational task not directly attached to a requirement.
+- `OPTIONAL`: a truly optional task; it does not block scoped G5. This classification is a claim, not proof of authorization to drop a requirement.
+- `DEFERRED` / `OUT_OF_SCOPE`: excluded by an actual scoped decision; record `scope_decision_ref` referencing a `DECISION` artifact, whose author remains externally unverified by the CLI.
+- `UNKNOWN` or omitted: preserves legacy data; unbound non-DONE tasks return `INCONCLUSIVE`, so a missed required task is not silently hidden by default.
+
+Any task linked to an applicable `MUST/MUST_NOT` requirement is mandatory regardless of its own optional classification. Its dependencies are also required for the G5 closure. Scope classification never changes original request text, authoritative requirements or owner decisions.
